gin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 9 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(3-45) \\\\  & =126.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440779 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440779 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131255" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440779 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440779 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -11 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{22}$ equal to zero.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440779 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4d57bf97-1629-5c5b-aa31-076c598fe8ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440779 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{22}=2$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -11 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440780 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440780 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132020" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440780 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440780 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & 12 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -8 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 5 & -6\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of ${a}_{21}$ equal to zero.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440780 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "51f6ebb7-f4d6-54f8-92af-8a0f13b34712" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440780 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's make entries to the right of ${a}_{21}=2$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & 12 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -8 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 5 & -6\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 &