186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551247 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries below ${a}_{14}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551247 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "231b9e48-9ef0-506b-a5a1-fc73da681086" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551247 #edb/ref 1074 "Using elementary row operations, let's make entries below ${a}_{14}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -13 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -7 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -13 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -7 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+4}|\\begin{aligned}6 & -13 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}6 & -13 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 6\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -1 \\\\ 9 & -7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-6(35-(-9)) \\\\  & =-264.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551268 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551268 #edb/ref 1069 "q-91219" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551268 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551268 #edb/ref 